// Pull request: #6092 Add ADS abuse and signed-binary LOLBIN detection rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6092
// Pull request author: einlamye
// Change: new rule
// Title: Remote File Download Via Signed Microsoft LOLBin
// Sigma ID: 318e685d-c51b-4488-8f12-80e355542510
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects several signed Microsoft binaries (xsd.exe, msoxmled.exe, ECMangen.exe,
//   VSLaunchBrowser.exe, dtutil.exe, WinProj.exe) being used to download or copy a file from a
//   remote URL or UNC path - a Living-Off-The-Land ingress tool transfer technique.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of these tools with UNC paths in enterprise environments (tune the UNC indicator if noisy)
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/xsd/
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Msoxmled/
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/ECMangen/
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/VsLaunchBrowser/
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Dtutil/
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Winproj/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/c5875f6ddd2f5087d0f0a63a34a2ed4468a9d328/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_ms_signed_remote_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\xsd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\msoxmled.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\ECMangen.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\VSLaunchBrowser.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\dtutil.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\winproj.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ftp://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\\\")
